d.\n  - positive reinforcement training class: Audrey is going to attend a positive reinforcement training class; she saw the flyer at her local pet store and met a friendly dog there.\n  - dog: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon for grooming. Andrew adopted another dog recently, managing with two dogs currently, and asked Audrey for multi-dog owner tips.\n  - workshop about bonding with my pet: Audrey heard about a positive reinforcement training class workshop at her local pet store and met a friendly dog there. Andrew expressed interest.\n  - four dogs: Audrey cherishes her four dogs, who always make her smile and give love. She has a tattoo of them and recently returned to the tattoo parlor for more drawings on it.\n  - dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon; they looked cute, groomed, and had shiny coats. Andrew has two dogs, Toby and Buddy. They are considered family members.\n  - obstacles: Audrey's pups are facing obstacles in agility classes, which Andrew finds impressive. Audrey saw a behaviorist last Wed for the dogs' abnormal behavior and got tips to try.\n  - neighbors' dogs: Audrey organized a doggy playdate with the neighbors' dogs, and seeing them wag their tails was sweet.\n  - dog training course: Audrey is taking a challenging but rewarding dog training course; it's a big time sink but her dogs are already doing great and improving.\n  - Audrey: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday, noting they looked cute with shiny coats, behaved well, and were happy and safe.\n  - pet salon: Audrey took her four dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; the dogs were excited, looked cute, and behaved well.\n  - Audrey's dogs: Audrey took her dogs to the pet salon last Friday for grooming; they looked cute with shiny coats and behaved well there.\n  - My dogs: Audrey's dogs enjoy meeting new people. They recently had grooming and look soft and fluffy.\n  - city dogs: Audrey's city dogs love trying new parks and trails and go on ad