racters and dialogue I wrote being acted out: Joanna experienced seeing all of the characters and dialogue she wrote being acted out, which was rewarding and the third time this has happened to her.\n  - writing inspiration: Joanna uses taking breaks and self-care for writing inspiration to maintain inspiration and mental health, seeking balance.\n  - rejection letter: Joanna received a generic rejection letter without much feedback from a major company after finishing her screenplay, which made her feel bummed out and disheartened.\n  - moments: Joanna remembers moments that bring happiness and remind her that life is great.\n  - writing gig: Joanna had an audition yesterday for a writing gig, feeling a mix of excitement and anxiety afterward. Nate previously encouraged her, noting her hard work and passion.\n  - the last one: Joanna is inspired to write a story about a thirty-year-old woman on a self-discovery journey after a loss, similar to 'the last one'.\n  - journal: Joanna uses her journal as her rock while she is busy with writing projects, finding it helps her express feelings and heal.\n  - fond memories: Joanna encourages looking back on fond memories, stating it is such a blessing.\n  - drama: Joanna felt inspired to write a drama after hiking on amazing trails in her town.\n  - love story: Joanna is writing a movie script for a love story that involves many challenges; she is working hard and hopes to see it on the big screen.\n  - writers group: Joanna shared her book with her writers group last week and received great feedback. She recently finished a cute little bookmark for one of the ladies at her writing club.\n  - Writing and creative projects: Joanna is busy with writing projects, which she finds to be a mix of highs and lows. Her journal is a major source of support for her writing endeavors.\n  - feedback: Joanna received positive feedback that people are connecting with her writing, which Nate mentioned.\n  - moods: Joanna is finding comfort