s that animals can be peaceful and joyful. (event_time: 2023-10-13T16:22:00Z)\n  - Volunteering with animals involves interacting with animals. (event_time: 2023-07-27T15:52:00Z)\n  - Andrew learned a lot about animals (event_time: 2023-10-01T19:09:00Z)\n  - Nature brings joy to Andrew's dogs (event_time: 2023-06-13T17:23:00Z)\n</FACTS>\n\n# These are the most relevant entities\n# ENTITY_NAME: entity summary\n<ENTITIES>\n  - animals: Andrew acknowledged the peaceful and joyful nature of animals, referencing potential adventures for Audrey's furry buddies.\n  - nature: Audrey saw an animal behaviorist due to her dogs acting abnormally. Andrew enjoyed a bike ride in a cool park outside of town, surrounded by nature.\n  - nature reserve: Andrew is heading to a nature reserve this weekend to reconnect with the outdoors.\n  - birds: Andrew enjoys watching birds in nature and reads books about ecological systems. Audrey has not mentioned birds.\n  - nature day: Andrew is looking forward to a nature day with the 'fur babies'.\n  - woods: Andrew is looking for a place near the woods so he can stay close to nature and provide a large open space for a dog to run around.\n  - volunteering with animals: Andrew found volunteering with animals very rewarding, but can no longer volunteer at the shelter, though he remains dedicated to making a difference.\n  - special moments: Andrew attempts to capture special moments, like adorable animals playing in the park with vibrant colors, to share the rewarding and happy feeling with others.\n  - Scout: Andrew feels lucky to have Scout, one of his furry friends. Audrey previously suggested slowly introducing Scout to Toby and Buddy.\n  - human being: Andrew stated that human beings need to look after nature because everything in nature is connected.\n  - weekend: Andrew plans to go camping over the weekend with his girlfriend, Toby, to enjoy nature, following a recent break where he visited a new cafe.\n  - the nature: Andrew enjoyed a re