ng her a sense of calm.\n  - she: Deborah enjoyed when 'she' baked her pineapple birthday cakes as a child, which made her feel special. Jolene has a cherished pet referred to as 'she'.\n  - animals: Jolene mentioned that pets have been a nice distraction and Deborah affirmed that animals bring happiness, comfort, teach responsibility, and help during tough times.\n  - Susie: Jolene mentioned that Susie is a great companion. Jolene has had Susie for two years.\n  - creature: Jolene bought a new aquarium the day before yesterday and now has a calm creature named Seraphim in it.\n  - Jolene: Jolene attended an awesome yoga retreat where she enjoyed a peaceful setting and an amazing sunrise view. She values catching up with friends like Deborah.\n  - Walking Dead: Jolene and others are planning to play \"Walking Dead\" next Saturday.\n  - Jolene and her partner: Jolene and her partner went scuba diving last Friday and found a cool spot to explore. Jolene also shared a picture of herself and her partner at a music festival last year.\n  - friends: Jolene had dinner and drinks with her friends the night before last. Jolene mentioned her pals are keeping her company. Deborah attended a music festival with pals and danced.\n  - loving owner: Jolene became the loving owner of someone or something, as mentioned by herself.\n  - Jolene and Anna: Deborah mentioned Anna got her a tasty vegan stir-fry (tofu, veg, ginger, soy sauce). Jolene mentioned doing yoga and meditation last Friday for me-time.\n  - them: Jolene has been doing 'them' sporadically for about 3 years and they have had a real positive effect on her.\n  - things that bring you joy: Deborah advises Jolene to make time for 'things that bring you joy' to experience joy.\n  - partner de Jolene: Jolene and her partner planned to play console games together.\n  - Jolene's partner: Jolene's partner has values that encourage pursuing creative endeavors. They recently returned from a trip to Rio de Janeiro with Jolene, w